<title>CHINA: China's Changyu to offer 80 mln B shares in 1997.</title>
<headline>China's Changyu to offer 80 mln B shares in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wine producer Changyu Group Co, based in Yantai in China's Shandong province, will offer and list 80 million B shares in 1997, a company official said on Friday.</p>
<p>The plan has already won official approval, she said, but declined to give further details.</p>
<p>The Changyu Group expected to raise 300 million yuan from the issue and use the money to expand production and buy two small firms, the International Business Daily said.</p>
<p>($1.0=8.3 yuan)</p>
</text>
